20. Explain Heartbeats, Session Timeout and Max Poll Interval.
Answer
Heartbeat

Consumer periodically tells broker:

I am Alive

session.timeout.ms

Maximum time broker waits for heartbeat.

Example:

session.timeout.ms=45000


If no heartbeat for 45 sec:

Consumer Dead
Rebalance Triggered

max.poll.interval.ms

Maximum processing time between poll calls.

Example:

max.poll.interval.ms=300000


(5 minutes)

If exceeded:

Consumer Removed From Group
Rebalance Starts

Bonus Questions (Extremely Asked)
What is max.poll.records?
Answer

Maximum records returned per poll.

Example:

max.poll.records=500

poll()


returns maximum 500 records.

Useful for controlling memory usage.

Difference Between Session Timeout and Max Poll Interval?
session.timeout.ms
Checks Consumer Health


Based on Heartbeats.

max.poll.interval.ms
Checks Processing Time


Based on Poll Frequency.

